  "slug": "dynamics-somatic-l1-19d0",
  "summary": "New preprints pair single-cell and long-read assays to quantify somatic L1 retrotransposition in neurons alongside other genomic and epigenomic variability.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is measuring somatic and inter-individual genomic variation at single-cell or single-molecule resolution. LUSTRE maps L1 insertion sites in ~17,600 adult human neurons to estimate somatic retrotransposition rates. Related items extend this theme to other layers: assembly-independent k-mer estimation of Yq12 satellite size across 1,597 males, ChIMe-seq joint profiling of histone modifications, DNA methylation and nucleosome positioning, and COMET assignment of bulk long-read reads to cell types by methylation. Others characterize variability itself: genome folding differences between pluripotent and differentiated cells, and continuous karyotypic fluctuation in acral melanoma linked to MMBIR repair. These are heterogeneous in system, but share a move toward resolving variability that bulk or assembly-based approaches obscure.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
